    "https://www.morningside.edu/about/employment/assistant-professor-of-special-education": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Special Education",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Special Education | Morningside University Skip to main menu Skip to content Assistant Professor of Special Education St. Luke’s College to join Morningside University. Read the full press release and FAQs Register for Senior Visit Day : Fall (Oct. 23 or Nov. 13) | Winter (Dec. 4 or Jan. 29) Admissions Start Your Experience At Morningside, you don't just apply for a degree, you embark on a journey to shape your identity, broaden your perspectives, and prepare for a successful future. Admissions Home Undergraduate Students Undergraduate Admissions Visit Morningside Apply to Morningside Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Returning Students Graduate Students Graduate Admissions Graduate Business Graduate Education Graduate Nursing Cost & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Access to Mside Siouxland Proud, Mside Bound Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Elementary Education (Online) RN to BSN (Online) Why Morningside? Sioux City Values & Outcomes Our Guarantee Stang Stories Contact Admissions Academics Shape Your Future With a commitment to lifelong learning, Morningside is a hub for rigorous academic inquiry and scholarly excellence providing students the knowledge they need to succeed. Academics Home Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Explore more than 65+ majors and pre-professional programs Graduate Programs Post-Bachelor's degrees and certificates Bachelor's Completion Programs Non-traditional student Bachelor degrees High School Student Programs Programs for current high school students Academic Opportunities Internships & Externships Study Abroad & May Term Schools & Departments Academic Schools School of Agriculture & Aviation School of Arts & Sciences Rosen School of Business Nylen School of Nursing & Health Sciences Sharon Walker School of Education School of Visual & Performing Arts Academic Resources Academic Calendars Library Academic Support Career & Alumni Support Research Information Technology Academic Catalogs Registrar Athletics Student Life + Arts Live and Learn With a commitment to lifelong learning, Morningside is a hub for rigorous academic inquiry and scholarly excellence providing students the knowledge they need to succeed. Student Life + Arts Home Life at Morningside Living on Campus Eating on Campus Campus Services Campus Ministry Campus Safety & Security Disability Services Information Technology Student Health & Wellness Athletic & Fitness Facilities Get Involved Volunteering & Engagement Siouxland Community Leadership Development Arts at Morningside Performing Arts Choral Music Instrumental Music Theatre Camps, Festivals, Workshops Christmas at Morningside CODA Legacy Awards Visual Arts Future Students Current Students Alumni & Friends Faculty/Staff Visit Apply Give Search Morningside Undergraduate programs | Graduate programs Faculty/staff directory | Contact us Morningside University / About Morningside / Employment / Assistant Professor of Special Education Morningside Employment Assistant Professor of Special Education September 4, 2026 SHARE ON: The Sharon Walker School of Education at Morningside University invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Special Education to provide instruction and support for initial licensure and endorsement special education programs in the unit. This position is a nine-month appointment beginning August 16, 2027. The Sharon Walker School of Education focuses exclusively on preparing future educators and providing advanced study for current educators, serving more than 1,000 students each year across undergraduate, adult, and graduate programs both on campus and online. The School offers traditional initial licensure programs for undergraduate students in elementary, special education, art and music education, and secondary education, as well as 14 MAT programs, including 4 initial licensure graduate MAT degree programs and 13 advanced practice endorsements. Of these, graduate special education programs have the highest enrollments. Morningside University is one of three institutions in the state of Iowa approved to offer initial licensure through the Iowa Teacher Intern program, and the only program approved to offer Special Education as a Teacher Intern program. In addition, Morningside University is one of eight institutions in Iowa to offer the K-12 Special Education, All undergraduate major. The Assistant Professor in Special Education provides instruction and support for the special education initial licensure and endorsement undergraduate and graduate programs across the unit. This is a full time, tenure track position with an annual teaching load of 24 credits. Responsibilities: Teach special education courses designed to meet the requirements for Iowa Special Education Instructional Strategist I and II, including mild/moderate methods, language development and communication disorders, methods of Behavior Disorder and Learning Disabilities or Intellectual Disabilities, assessment, and/or applied behavior analysis. Course assignments may be undergraduate and/or graduate courses, delivered in any of these formats: face to face, hybrid, and online. Assist with the development, design, and leadership of a new delivery format and clinical model for the undergraduate K-12 All Special Education major. Advise and mentor undergraduate special education majors and in-service graduate students seeking special education endorsements. Provide content oversight for special education curriculum and assessment in the unit, serving as an academic coordinator (course author and mentor) for select special education courses, as needed. Participate in service to the unit and university, and engage in professional development. Demonstrate the qualities of an effective educator, a commitment to implementing high-quality education programs that meet and exceed state standards, and an enthusiastic dedication to teacher preparation. Teach a May Term course once every three years. Qualifications: An earned doctorate in special education, curriculum and instruction, education, or closely related field. (ABD will be considered if completion is expected within one year.) Special education licensure, (Iowa Special Education Instructional Strategist I and II, preferred) and special education K-12 teaching experience. Preference given to candidates with additional experience as a Special Education Instructional Coach. Outstanding educational and instructional technology skills, experience using learning management systems, electronic portfolio systems, and remote learning platforms. Demonstrated experience and/or commitment to creating inclusive learning environments and curricula for a diverse student body, including awareness of current practices that support underrepresented populations. Additional licensure/endorsements in literacy, ELL, talented and gifted, or educational administration, preferred. Prior experience in online teaching, adult education, and/or graduate programs, preferred. Prior teaching experience in higher education teacher preparation programs, preferred. Morningside is a private university located in Sioux City, Iowa, that serves over 2,000 students from almost all 50 states and more than 30 countries. It was established in 1894 by The United Methodist Church, an affiliation it continues to maintain, and Chad W. Benson serves as its President. The main campus comprises 69 acres nestled in a serene, park-like setting in the heart of Iowa’s fourth largest city. Lags Farm and Sioux Gateway Airport are both nearby extensions of the campus that serve the School of Agriculture and Aviation. Morningside’s largest undergraduate programs are education, nursing, and business, and the Sharon Walker School of Education, Nylen School of Nursing and the Rosen School of Business all offer well-established online post-baccalaureate and graduate program options for nontraditional and graduate students. A strong commitment to experiential learning has enabled Morningside University to maintain a remarkable 99% job and graduate school placement rate for its undergraduate graduates over the past decade. Morningside University is home to the Mustangs Athletic Department, which fields 28 varsity sports and is a proud member of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) and the Great Plains Athletic Conference (GPAC). Residential undergraduate students may also enjoy more than 50 student-led clubs and organizations or choose to get involved with the School of Visual and Performing Arts regardless of their major. Learn more about Morningside University at morningside.edu Review of applications for the position will begin immediately and will continue until filled. For fullest consideration, applicant materials should be received by October 16, 2026 .  Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Successful completion of a background check and education verification is required. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, sex, religion, creed, race, color, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, genetic information, national origin, or other characteristics protected by state and federal law. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact the Director of Human Resources at welp@morningside.edu. Apply online only by submitting an email to facultysearch@morningside.edu entering Special Education Search in the subject line and attaching a PDF or Microsoft Word files for the following documents: A cover letter, current curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, and the names and contact information for three persons to provide professional recommendations. If the letters of recommendation are not included in the application, they must be submitted electronically to the “facultysearch” email address provided above. Questions about the position may be addressed to Stacey Brown, Department Head, Sharon Walker School of Education, browns@morningside.edu SEE ALL EMPLOYMENT POSTINGS Main Menu Information For Future Students Current Students Alumni & Friends Faculty/Staff Admissions Academics Athletics Student Life + Arts Visit Apply Give About Morningside Mside Store News Events Employment Sitemap Undergraduate Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Overview Visit Morningside Apply to Morningside Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Returning Students Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Overview Elementary Education (Online) RN to BSN (Online) Graduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Overview Graduate Business Graduate Education Graduate Nursing Why Morningside? Why Morningside? Overview Sioux City Values & Outcomes Our Guarantee Stang Stories Admissions Admissions Overview Undergraduate Admissions Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Graduate Admissions Tuition & Fees Access to Mside Siouxland Proud, Mside Bound Contact Admissions Why Morningside? Academic Schools Academic Schools Overview School of Agriculture & Aviation School of Arts & Sciences Rosen School of Business Nylen School of Nursing & Health Sciences Sharon Walker School of Education School of Visual & Performing Arts Academics Academics Overview Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Bachelor's Completion Programs Academic Schools High School Student Programs Academic Calendars Library Study Abroad & May Term Internships & Externships Career & Alumni Support Academic Support Research Information Technology Academic Catalogs Registrar Campus Services Campus Services Overview Campus Ministry Campus Safety & Security Disability Services Information Technology Student Health & Wellness Athletic & Fitness Facilities Performing Arts Performing Arts Overview Choral Music Instrumental