    "https://www.morningside.edu/about/employment/assistant-associate-professor-of-management-business-administration": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Management/Business Administration",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Management/Business Administration | Morningside University Skip to main menu Skip to content Assistant/Associate Professor of Management/Business Administration St. Luke’s College to join Morningside University. Read the full press release and FAQs Register for Senior Visit Day : Fall (Oct. 23 or Nov. 13) | Winter (Dec. 4 or Jan. 29) Admissions Start Your Experience At Morningside, you don't just apply for a degree, you embark on a journey to shape your identity, broaden your perspectives, and prepare for a successful future. Admissions Home Undergraduate Students Undergraduate Admissions Visit Morningside Apply to Morningside Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Returning Students Graduate Students Graduate Admissions Graduate Business Graduate Education Graduate Nursing Cost & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Access to Mside Siouxland Proud, Mside Bound Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Elementary Education (Online) RN to BSN (Online) Why Morningside? Sioux City Values & Outcomes Our Guarantee Stang Stories Contact Admissions Academics Shape Your Future With a commitment to lifelong learning, Morningside is a hub for rigorous academic inquiry and scholarly excellence providing students the knowledge they need to succeed. Academics Home Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Explore more than 65+ majors and pre-professional programs Graduate Programs Post-Bachelor's degrees and certificates Bachelor's Completion Programs Non-traditional student Bachelor degrees High School Student Programs Programs for current high school students Academic Opportunities Internships & Externships Study Abroad & May Term Schools & Departments Academic Schools School of Agriculture & Aviation School of Arts & Sciences Rosen School of Business Nylen School of Nursing & Health Sciences Sharon Walker School of Education School of Visual & Performing Arts Academic Resources Academic Calendars Library Academic Support Career & Alumni Support Research Information Technology Academic Catalogs Registrar Athletics Student Life + Arts Live and Learn With a commitment to lifelong learning, Morningside is a hub for rigorous academic inquiry and scholarly excellence providing students the knowledge they need to succeed. Student Life + Arts Home Life at Morningside Living on Campus Eating on Campus Campus Services Campus Ministry Campus Safety & Security Disability Services Information Technology Student Health & Wellness Athletic & Fitness Facilities Get Involved Volunteering & Engagement Siouxland Community Leadership Development Arts at Morningside Performing Arts Choral Music Instrumental Music Theatre Camps, Festivals, Workshops Christmas at Morningside CODA Legacy Awards Visual Arts Future Students Current Students Alumni & Friends Faculty/Staff Visit Apply Give Search Morningside Undergraduate programs | Graduate programs Faculty/staff directory | Contact us Morningside University / About Morningside / Employment / Assistant/Associate Professor of Management/Business Administration Morningside Employment Assistant/Associate Professor of Management/Business Administration August 25, 2026 SHARE ON: Assistant/Associate Professor – Management/Business Administration (Tenure Track) Institution: Morningside University, Rosen School of Business Location: Sioux City, Iowa Application Deadline: For full consideration, apply by September 30, 2026. Morningside University’s Rosen School of Business seeks applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor in Management/Business Administration to begin August 16, 2027. This is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track faculty position. Strong candidates will be those who are eager to share their knowledge, skills and experiences with Morningside students, while actively contributing to the School’s projects and initiatives. For this position, there is a particular need for applicants with experience in and a passion for areas, including: AI in business, business ethics, entrepreneurship and innovation, international business, leadership, management, project and operations management, and/or small business management. General Description of Faculty Role The business faculty at Morningside University are an innovative and collegial group of educators focused on student success. We support students with diverse career goals, including students pursuing careers across offered disciplines, including accounting, business administration, economics, entrepreneurship, finance, management, marketing, and sports management. The faculty serve as professional educators, most of whom have rich industry experiences. We strive to provide high-quality education, academic advising, and mentorship for all Morningside University students, while also engaging in innovative research and meaningful service. We regularly collaborate with faculty across our institution, professional and business organizations, and industry leaders. At this time, we are seeking a new colleague who can demonstrate an ongoing commitment to high-quality teaching, be energetic, engaging, student-focused, and have strong interpersonal and communication skills. We want a colleague who can demonstrate a sincere commitment to creating an inclusive learning environment for Morningside students. The ideal candidate will have values that align with Morningside’s mission, vision, and community standards and a genuine desire to support our students, university, and school. We are invested in the success of our students and are searching for candidates who will be excited to join our team and amplify our existing efforts and energy. At Morningside University, there are tremendous opportunities to innovate, contribute, and make lasting a difference. Teaching Load and Course Concentration A full teaching load is 24 credits per academic year. Our semester-long undergraduate classes are 4-credit hours courses. Some 2-credit courses are offered for either the first half (FH) or second half (SH) of the semester. MBA-level classes are concentrated 3-credit hour courses that are offered either FH or SH of any given semester (with additional MBA-level courses offered during the summer). Opportunities to teach overload and/or teach during the summer session may be possible, dependent upon the student demand and approval by Academic Affairs. Qualifications A Doctoral degree in Business Management is preferred. With appropriate experience, candidates who are ABD will be considered. Relevant experience and preferred qualifications include: University-level teaching experience Experience mentoring or advising students Strong interpersonal and communication skills Experience with (or eagerness to learn) modern instructional technologies Prior for-profit, not-for-profit, or governmental work experience During the academic year, faculty are expected to work on campus in Sioux City, Iowa. About the Rosen School of Business The School currently offers majors in Business Administration, Finance, Management, Marketing, Managerial Accounting, Public Accounting, and Sports Management. Our School is proud to have a 99% placement rate for graduates and is experiencing growth across all its majors. There are over 400 students who have declared business majors. Many business students are actively engaged in on-campus activities, including athletics, student clubs, the arts, and on-campus student employment. The current faculty have many years of prior experience working in the industry or public sectors. We strive to be innovative, practical and forward-thinking—in fact, we have just added a new required course focusing on AI for all business majors. Business faculty regularly collaborate with faculty and staff across the institution on research, service and events. The School serves as a local and regional resource to business organizations, and we are actively working to elevate our profile as a resource for area business leaders throughout the region. Our MBA program was launched less than two years ago, and our student enrollment numbers have surpassed our expectations. This program is flexible and designed to fit into their already busy lives. Our MBA program offers students a range of concentrations, currently including:  AI; business analytics; cyber security; finance; healthcare administration; and project, operations, & manufacturing. In June 2026, we broke ground to construct a new academic building to house the Rosen School of Business.  Honeck Freyman Hall will be a state-of-the-art learning environment designed to foster innovation, creativity and excellence.  The 40,000-square-foot facility will feature advanced classrooms, collaborative workspaces and cutting-edge technology to meet the evolving needs of students, faculty and the business community. About Morningside University Morningside University is a private university located in Sioux City, Iowa, that serves over 2,000 students from almost all 50 states and more than 30 countries. It was established in 1894 by The United Methodist Church, an affiliation it continues to maintain, and Chad Benson serves as its President. The main campus comprises 69 acres nestled in a serene, park-like setting in the heart of Iowa’s fourth largest city. Lags Farm and Sioux Gateway Airport are both nearby extensions of the campus that serve the School of Agriculture and Aviation. Morningside’s largest undergraduate programs are education, nursing, and business, and the Sharon Walker School of Education, Nylen School of Nursing and the Rosen School of Business all offer well-established online post-baccalaureate and graduate program options for nontraditional and graduate students. A strong commitment to experiential learning has enabled Morningside University to maintain a remarkable 99% job and graduate school placement rate for its undergraduate graduates over the past decade. Morningside University is home to the Mustangs Athletic Department, which fields 28 varsity sports and is a proud member of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) and the Great Plains Athletic Conference (GPAC). Residential undergraduate students may also enjoy more than 50 student-led clubs and organizations or choose to get involved with the School of Visual and Performing Arts regardless of their major. Our Mission The Morningside University experience cultivates a passion for lifelong learning and a dedication to ethical leadership and civic responsibility . How Do I Apply? To apply, please send an email to facultysearch@morningside.edu entering “Faculty Search – Management/Bus. Admin.” in the subject line and attaching PDF or Microsoft Word files for the following documents: A cover letter of interest highlighting relevant experiences that meet the position’s required qualifications and desired qualifications A current curriculum vitae 1-page statement of teaching philosophy 1-page statement of research interests Contact details for three professional references Semifinalists and finalists may be asked to provide additional materials. For full consideration, apply by September 30, 2026. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Successful completion of a background check and education verification is required. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, sex, religion, creed, race, color, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, genetic information, national origin, or other characteristics protected by state and federal law. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact the Director of Human Resources at welp@morningside.edu. If you have any questions about this position or working in Morningside University’s Rosen School of Business, please contact Dr. Paula Kueter, (p) 712-274-5182, (e) kueterp@morningside .edu . To learn more about working at Morningside University, visit: www.morningside.edu/about/employment SEE ALL EMPLOYMENT POSTINGS Main Menu Information For Future Students Current Students Alumni & Friends Faculty/Staff Admissions Academics Athletics Student Life + Arts Visit Apply Give About Morningside Mside Store News Events Employment Sitemap Undergraduate Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Overview Visit Morningside Apply to Morningside Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Returning Students Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Overview Elementary Education (Online) RN to BSN (Online) Graduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Overview Graduate Business Graduate Education Graduate Nursing Why Morningside? Why Morningside? Overview Sioux City Values & Outcomes Our Guarantee Stang Stories Admissions Admissions Overview Undergraduate Admissions Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Graduate Admissions Tuition & Fees Access to Mside Siouxland Proud, Mside Bound Contact Admissions Why Morningside? Academic Schools Academic Schools Overview School of Agriculture & Aviation School of Arts & Sciences Rosen School of Business Nylen School of Nursing & Health Sciences Sharon Walker School of Education School of Visual & Performing Arts Academics Academics Overview Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Bachelor's Completion Programs Academic Schools High School Student Programs Academic Calendars Library Study Abroad & May Term Internships & Externships Career & Alumni Support Academic Support Research Information Technology Academic Catalogs Registrar Campus Services Campus Services Overview Campus Ministry Campus Safety & Security Disability Services Information Technology Student Health & Wellness Athletic & Fitness Facilities Performing Arts Performing Arts Overview Choral Music Instrumental Music Theatre Camps, Festivals, Workshops Christmas at Morningside CODA Legacy Awards Student Life + Arts Student Life + Arts Overview Living on Campus Eating on Campus Campus Services Performing Arts Visual Arts Volunteering & Engagement Siouxland Community Leadership Development Site Footer Contact Information Morningside University 1501 Morningside Avenue Sioux City, Iowa 51106 712-274-5000 Footer Menu Visit Apply Give Future Students Current Students Alumni & Friends Admissions Academics Athletics Student Life + Arts About Morningside Social Links News Events Copyright and Disclosures © 2026 Morningside University Consumer Information Privacy Statement Professional Licensure Disclosures Title IX Employment Sitemap"
