    "https://www.morningside.edu/about/employment/assistant-professor-of-mathematics": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics | Morningside University Skip to main menu Skip to content Assistant Professor of Mathematics St. Luke’s College to join Morningside University. Read the full press release and FAQs Register for Senior Visit Day : Fall (Oct. 23 or Nov. 13) | Winter (Dec. 4 or Jan. 29) Admissions Start Your Experience At Morningside, you don't just apply for a degree, you embark on a journey to shape your identity, broaden your perspectives, and prepare for a successful future. Admissions Home Undergraduate Students Undergraduate Admissions Visit Morningside Apply to Morningside Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Returning Students Graduate Students Graduate Admissions Graduate Business Graduate Education Graduate Nursing Cost & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Access to Mside Siouxland Proud, Mside Bound Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Elementary Education (Online) RN to BSN (Online) Why Morningside? Sioux City Values & Outcomes Our Guarantee Stang Stories Contact Admissions Academics Shape Your Future With a commitment to lifelong learning, Morningside is a hub for rigorous academic inquiry and scholarly excellence providing students the knowledge they need to succeed. Academics Home Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Explore more than 65+ majors and pre-professional programs Graduate Programs Post-Bachelor's degrees and certificates Bachelor's Completion Programs Non-traditional student Bachelor degrees High School Student Programs Programs for current high school students Academic Opportunities Internships & Externships Study Abroad & May Term Schools & Departments Academic Schools School of Agriculture & Aviation School of Arts & Sciences Rosen School of Business Nylen School of Nursing & Health Sciences Sharon Walker School of Education School of Visual & Performing Arts Academic Resources Academic Calendars Library Academic Support Career & Alumni Support Research Information Technology Academic Catalogs Registrar Athletics Student Life + Arts Live and Learn With a commitment to lifelong learning, Morningside is a hub for rigorous academic inquiry and scholarly excellence providing students the knowledge they need to succeed. Student Life + Arts Home Life at Morningside Living on Campus Eating on Campus Campus Services Campus Ministry Campus Safety & Security Disability Services Information Technology Student Health & Wellness Athletic & Fitness Facilities Get Involved Volunteering & Engagement Siouxland Community Leadership Development Arts at Morningside Performing Arts Choral Music Instrumental Music Theatre Camps, Festivals, Workshops Christmas at Morningside CODA Legacy Awards Visual Arts Future Students Current Students Alumni & Friends Faculty/Staff Visit Apply Give Search Morningside Undergraduate programs | Graduate programs Faculty/staff directory | Contact us Morningside University / About Morningside / Employment / Assistant Professor of Mathematics Morningside Employment Assistant Professor of Mathematics October 13, 2026 SHARE ON: Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Mathematics The Department of Mathematical Sciences at Morningside University is seeking applications for a tenure-track assistant professor in mathematics, to begin August 16, 2027. Responsibilities : Teaching load is 24 credits per academic year which includes a May term once every 3 years. Teaching courses at all undergraduate levels of mathematics, including introductory statistics. Qualifications : Applicants with a PhD in Mathematics or a closely related field are preferred, ABD will be considered, Master’s Degree required. Experience teaching undergraduates at various levels, mentoring undergraduate research students, and engaging with students from diverse backgrounds preferred. About Morningside : Morningside is a private university located in Sioux City, Iowa, that serves over 2,000 students from almost all 50 states and more than 30 countries. It was established in 1894 by The United Methodist Church, an affiliation it continues to maintain, and Chad W. Benson serves as its President. The main campus comprises 69 acres nestled in a serene, park-like setting in the heart of Iowa’s fourth largest city. Lags Farm and Sioux Gateway Airport are both nearby extensions of the campus that serve the School of Agriculture and Aviation. Morningside’s largest undergraduate programs are education, nursing, and business, and the Sharon Walker School of Education, Nylen School of Nursing and the Rosen School of Business all offer well-established online post-baccalaureate and graduate program options for nontraditional and graduate students. A strong commitment to experiential learning has enabled Morningside University to maintain a remarkable 99% job and graduate school placement rate for its undergraduate graduates over the past decade. Morningside University is home to the Mustangs Athletic Department, which fields 28 varsity sports and is a proud member of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) and the Great Plains Athletic Conference (GPAC). Residential undergraduate students may also enjoy more than 50 student-led clubs and organizations or choose to get involved with the School of Visual and Performing Arts regardless of their major. Learn more about Morningside University at morningside.edu Review of applications for the position will begin immediately and will continue until filled. Applications received by November 13, 2026 will receive full consideration. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Successful completion of a background check and education verification are required. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, sex, religion, creed, race, color, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, genetic information, national origin, or other characteristics protected by state and federal law. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact the Director of Human Resources at welp@morningside.edu. Apply on-line by submitting an email to facultysearch@morningside.edu and put ‘Math Search’ in the subject line. Please attach a PDF or Microsoft Word files of the following documents: A cover letter Current curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy A brief statement of research interests The names and contact information for three people to provide professional recommendations. If you have any questions about the position, please don’t hesitate to contact Professor Dean Stevens, Department Head for Mathematical Sciences and search committee chair at stevens@morningside.edu. SEE ALL EMPLOYMENT POSTINGS Main Menu Information For Future Students Current Students Alumni & Friends Faculty/Staff Admissions Academics Athletics Student Life + Arts Visit Apply Give About Morningside Mside Store News Events Employment Sitemap Undergraduate Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Overview Visit Morningside Apply to Morningside Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Returning Students Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Overview Elementary Education (Online) RN to BSN (Online) Graduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Overview Graduate Business Graduate Education Graduate Nursing Why Morningside? Why Morningside? Overview Sioux City Values & Outcomes Our Guarantee Stang Stories Admissions Admissions Overview Undergraduate Admissions Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Graduate Admissions Tuition & Fees Access to Mside Siouxland Proud, Mside Bound Contact Admissions Why Morningside? Academic Schools Academic Schools Overview School of Agriculture & Aviation School of Arts & Sciences Rosen School of Business Nylen School of Nursing & Health Sciences Sharon Walker School of Education Scho